# Coach speech (Brazilian Portuguese): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "você"; the player's gender is
# unknown: no adjective or participle agrees with the player ("você estava ganhando", "você já pode
# passar para o nível...", never "pronto", "derrotado").
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   with their article ("a abertura", "o meio-jogo", "o final"): said as a subject
#                       or after a verb, or after "durante" (which does not contract); never after
#                       de / em / a / por ("no final" would need a contraction).
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement right after "Empate" ("Empate por repetição.").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase starting with the verb ("olhar o tabuleiro inteiro antes
#                       de jogar"), no adjective agreeing with the player; said after a colon, after
#                       "tente" or after "Lembre-se de".
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name in curly quotes, said after "nível": "o nível “Iniciante”".
# {opening:def} = the opening's name with its article ("a Defesa Siciliana"); plain {opening} after a
# colon or alone ("Abertura: Defesa Siciliana.").
# Percentages use the count form "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "oitenta e cinco por cento").
# Counts that may be zero (mistakes, inaccuracies, captures) are given after a label ("Erros: {m}"),
# not as "0 erro"; the number agrees with the label's noun: {n:f} for imprecisões, peças, capturas.
# Move numbers are cardinal: "no lance {n}" (spoken "no lance vinte e um").

